From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:24:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Limit the OWA RX clock to its documented
 parent

OWA_RX_CLK (0x1284) is described with three parents, the 200, 300 and
400 MHz outputs of PLL_PERI0 at mux values 0, 1 and 2. The A733 manual
lists only value 2, PERI0_400M; values 0 and 1 are reserved, and the
register resets to 0 (user manual section 4.1.6.190). Without a write
to the mux, the receiver clock runs from a reserved source, because
nothing selects PERI0_400M. Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: after boot
OWA_RX_CLK reads 0.

Describe the clock with its one documented parent and without the mux,
and select PERI0_400M in the probe, as the H616 driver does for its OHCI
12M clocks.

Not covered: OWA_TX keeps its three documented audio PLL parents.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on one board OWA_RX_CLK reads mux 2
(PERI0_400M) after boot instead of 0, and an OWA loop from TX to RX at
48 kHz received clean, locked data.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 700cae872ece..be50812f8c16 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -1211,16 +1211,16 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_M_HW_WITH_MUX_GATE(spdif_tx_clk, "spdif-tx", spdif_tx_parents,
 				    BIT(31),	/* gate */
 				    0);
 
-static const struct clk_hw *spdif_rx_parents[] = {
-	&pll_periph0_200M_clk.hw,
-	&pll_periph0_300M_clk.hw,
-	&pll_periph0_400M_clk.hw,
-};
-static SUNXI_CCU_M_HW_WITH_MUX_GATE(spdif_rx_clk, "spdif-rx", spdif_rx_parents, 0x1284,
-				    0, 5,	/* M */
-				    24, 3,	/* mux */
-				    BIT(31),	/* gate */
-				    0);
+/*
+ * Only mux value 2 (PERI0_400M) is documented, 0 and 1 are reserved: the
+ * probe selects it, the clock is described without its mux.
+ */
+#define SUN60I_A733_OWA_RX_CLK_REG	0x1284
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_HWS_WITH_GATE(spdif_rx_clk, "spdif-rx", pll_periph0_400M_hws,
+				 SUN60I_A733_OWA_RX_CLK_REG,
+				 0, 5,		/* M */
+				 BIT(31),	/* gate */
+				 0);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_spdif_clk, "bus-spdif", apb1_hws, 0x128c, BIT(0), 0);
 
@@ -2403,6 +2403,15 @@ static int sun60i_a733_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	val |= (1 << 20) | (4 << 16);
 	writel(val, reg + SUN60I_A733_PLL_AUDIO1_REG);
 
+	/*
+	 * OWA_RX_CLK resets to the reserved source 0. With a single parent
+	 * the clock framework never writes the mux, so select PERI0_400M.
+	 */
+	val = readl(reg + SUN60I_A733_OWA_RX_CLK_REG);
+	val &= ~GENMASK(26, 24);
+	val |= 2 << 24;
+	writel(val, reg + SUN60I_A733_OWA_RX_CLK_REG);
+
 	ret = devm_sunxi_ccu_probe(&pdev->dev, reg, &sun60i_a733_ccu_desc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
